  "description": "This is probably an Ayrton Zonda 9 Wash, a single-unit moving-head wash. A rectangular base, roughly 0.49 x 0.10 x 0.28 m, supports a U-shaped yoke with tilt pivots on each side of the head. The round-fronted head, about 0.5 m across, probably has heat-sink fins along its top. The yoke pans 570 degrees and the head tilts 270 degrees within it, both DMX-driven and not per head. The front is a flat lens disc of 37 rounded-hexagonal lenses in a hex flower: one centre, rings of 6, 12 and 18, separated by dark grid lines. Colour is probably five independently controllable cells, with the lenses sharing one colour set. These ring pixels are probably not modelled.",
